--no-ff`, `--squash` (including on conflict: HEAD stays unchanged and no merge state is recorded; resolve and stage conflicts, then plain `libra commit` creates one parent; `--continue`/`--abort`/`--restart` report `no merge in progress`), `--no-commit` (retains merge state, including conflicts, and finishes with a two-parent `merge --continue`), `--no-edit` (accepted no-op; Libra never opens an editor for merge), `--stat`/`-n`/`--no-stat` (last-wins toggle; `--stat` prints a post-merge diffstat of the merge's changes, the default is no diffstat), `--no-progress` (accepted no-op; Libra's merge renders no progress meter), `--verify-signatures` (verify the merged tip's PGP signature against the local vault key — like `tag -v`, only signatures made by this repository's vault key can be validated; no external keyring) / `--no-verify-signatures` (the default; toggle pair, last wins), `--no-rerere-autoupdate` (accepted no-op — its per-invocation override is not implemented; rerere IS auto-integrated when `rerere.enabled` is set, with staging always following `rerere.autoUpdate`), and `--no-gpg-sign` (accepted no-op; Libra's merge never signs the merge commit) supported; `merge.conflictStyle` supports `merge`/`diff3`/`zdiff3` and fails closed on unknown values; the default merge style re-diffs postimages to move common edges and runs longer than three lines outside markers, zdiff3 keeps the complete base block while trimming common postimage edges, and uniformly CRLF inputs produce CRLF marker lines; MG-11 adds `-X ignore-space-change|ignore-all-space|ignore-space-at-eol|ignore-cr-at-eol`, `-X renormalize|no-renormalize`, and strict phase-local `merge.renormalize` (text/eol attributes only; no arbitrary clean/smudge filter execution; external drivers receive renormalized but not whitespace-folded inputs); merge commits carry the configured `user.name`/`user.email` on every path (three-way, `--no-ff`, `-s ours`, `--continue`) and fail closed with the same identity error as `commit` when none is configured; Libra extensions: `--dry-run` (zero-write preview; exit 0 clean, exit 1 would-conflict), `--continue -m <msg>` (Git's `--continue` takes no arguments; Libra never opens an editor for merge, so `-m` is the only way to set a conflicted non-squash merge's message — it overrides the message recorded at merge start, and without it the stored message is replayed), and `--restart` (requires non-squash conflict state; abort then re-run the recorded target, replaying recovery-critical unrelated-history permission but not presentation/policy options); external strategies, `subtree`, explicit `-s octopus`, and strategy options outside `ours/theirs/ignore-space-change/ignore-all-space/ignore-space-at-eol/ignore-cr-at-eol/renormalize/no-renormalize`, `--rerere-autoupdate`, and `-S`/`--gpg-sign` deferred; submodules are a permanent non-goal (ADR-MG-01 / declined `D24`): a three-way merge that would have to ARBITRATE a `160000` gitlink — any side recording a different commit id than the merge base, including a side that added or removed it — is refused before any write with `LBR-UNSUPPORTED-001` naming the path, while a gitlink all three sides agree on is carried into the merge result verbatim instead of being silently dropped (`merge`, `rebase` and `cherry-pick` share one guard); `--autostash`/`--no-autostash` + `merge.autostash` hold tracked dirty state outside `stash list` across non-squash conflicts/restart and separately restore staged index + unstaged worktree, promoting a conflicting re-apply into the stash list; clean squash attempts autostash restoration as the command returns; conflicted squash instead saves the autostash directly in `stash list` without applying it, preserving the unresolved index and working tree for resolution and a plain commit before `stash pop` (save failure warns and retains the held sidecar); JSON adds `autostash: applied|stashed|kept`; lore.md 2.6 symmetric cross-op sequencer mutex remains enforced.; renames are