ge 1 (no stage 0) — an edited file is Git's modify/delete conflict relocated to that name (Git's modify/delete line printed too, the version left verbatim), a one-sided add the pure file/directory kind, an untouched file a clean deletion, a directory of only empty trees in the way only when the base had nothing at that path (Git's verbatim adoption of a new directory), `-X ours/theirs` leaving a modify/delete under a directory a conflict, a moved symlink staying a symlink — human lines only (JSON/machine stdout stays clean) and printed only once the merge is past its preflight, conflicts reported in path order, writes and removals never following a symlinked directory, a directory replaced by a file only when nothing but this merge's own files is inside it, an ignored file at either name replaced as Git replaces it while an untracked one refuses the merge, a moved symlink target kept byte-for-byte, discarding a moved file not yet possible (`libra rm` rejects unmerged paths), a non-squash merge's `--abort` removing the moved copy and pruning emptied directories; a directory that merges to nothing is not in the way; inside a criss-cross fold the file moves to `<path>~Temporary merge branch N` like Git at `call_depth > 0`; `--dry-run` JSON adds `conflict_kinds` (`content` / `modify-delete` / `file-directory` / `rename-rename` + `original_path`). A regular `commit` after resolving or `--no-commit` finishes the merge (two parents, saved message, then clear merge state / apply autostash); `--squash` leaves `SQUASH_MSG` for the following single-parent commit. Conflict markers use Git-form labels: `<<<<<<< HEAD` / `>>>>>>> <user-spelling>` (the merge target exactly as typed) and, under `diff3`, `||||||| <merge-base abbrev7>`.; reset clears an in-progress merge and keeps its autostash in the stash list; a plain commit concludes the in-progress merge; conflict markers name the merge target as typed worktree materialization is mode-aware — files are created with the entry mode