4102-COMPATIBILITY.md:213:| rev-parse | partial | strict revision/object parsing supports branch/tag/remote/full refs, `@`, `^N`/`~N`, typed peel `^{commit|tree|blob|tag|object}`, recursive `^{}`, numeric reflog selectors (`HEAD@{N}`/`@{N}`/`branch@{N}`), and repository-root `REV:path`, with SHA-1/SHA-256 object-id validation. `--verify` proves the resolved object exists; `--short[=<n>]`, `--abbrev-ref`, `--symbolic-full-name`, `--symbolic`, repository/path queries, `--sq`, output-filter modes, multiple `<SPEC>` arguments, and `--` separation are supported. `--git-dir`/`--absolute-git-dir`/`--is-inside-git-dir` return (and test) the CURRENT worktree's local gitdir: for the main worktree this is the shared `.libra`; for a linked worktree it is that worktree's own `.libra` (holding its private HEAD/index), not the shared common storage. **Intentional divergence:** combining `--verify`/`--short` with output-filter flags is LBR-CLI-002 / exit 129. Date reflog selectors, `@{-N}`, `@{upstream}`/`@{push}`, relative tree paths, `--abbrev=<n>`, and parseopt modes remain incomplete **Pseudo-refs are not resolvable names (deferred, plan-20260714 §C.5):** `ORIG_HEAD`, `MERGE_HEAD`, `CHERRY_PICK_HEAD`, `REVERT_HEAD`, `REBASE_HEAD` and `FETCH_HEAD` are NOT accepted as revisions — `rev-parse MERGE_HEAD` fails as an unknown revision rather than resolving one. Libra keeps that state in per-worktree database rows and sidecars, not in `GIT_DIR` files, and the internal `WorktreePseudoRefs` service (`src/internal/pseudo_ref.rs`) is the ONE projection of it — its per-worktree isolation is pinned by the `linked_pseudo_refs_resolve_per_worktree` regression; if these names ever become resolvable they will resolve through that service, per worktree. `ORIG_HEAD` is also NARROWER than Git's: it is the commit this worktree's sequence/bisect started from, and `reset`/`am` do not write it. |
